1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
This bundle has a Lightning cable,
but my phone uses USB-C.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:13,000
So the store refuses to take my money,
and puts the fix right where I am.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,000
OpenHands Commerce: an accessible shopping assistant
that checks your order before PayPal opens.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:27,000
I describe what I need in my own words,
using only the keyboard.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Then I pick the bundle with the wrong cable,
the mistake you'd only catch by reading closely.

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Payment is blocked, the reason is shown,
and the fix is the very next stop.

7
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:54,000
One key, same price, and the total,
including shipping and tax, is checked against my budget.

8
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Our server works out every price from the catalog
and decides what's safe to buy.

9
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:10,000
AI can help word the explanations, but it has no tools and can't touch money.
Today you're seeing our rule-based text, and the label says so.

10
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:35,000
[OWNER FOOTAGE: PayPal Sandbox login and Pay]
PayPal creates an order bound to that exact quote.
I confirm in PayPal Sandbox. It's test money only.

11
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:55,000
[OWNER FOOTAGE: verified receipt]
We capture once, then ask PayPal directly. The receipt says paid only when
PayPal reports it completed, for the amount I approved. Refreshing can't charge me twice.

12
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:59,000
If I cancel, it says nothing was charged
and keeps my order.

13
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:11,000
It works in high-contrast mode, at 400 percent zoom,
and with the keyboard alone.

14
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:22,000
OpenHands Commerce. The AI explains, the server decides,
and you stay in control.
